{# One client's last-hour sparkline, fetched on selection and slotted into that
   client's detail section by the map JS. `spark` is NetworkUsageChart::build()
   output (or null). Null renders NOTHING — not even whitespace — because the
   route's contract is "empty body = no history", which the JS turns into a note.

   Drawn like the history panel's usage chart: same .unifi-chart* classes (page
   CSS in the shell's stylesheets block — a fragment is re-injected and must not
   carry style or script tags), same geometry. The viewBox comes from the helper's
   constants because the points are already mapped into that box; only the
   rendered height differs, set inline (CSP allows style attributes) over the
   shell's 120px. preserveAspectRatio="none" squashes the box vertically, so the
   strokes opt out of scaling or they would thin to under a pixel at 48px.

   The SVG is aria-hidden: the visible ↓/↑ totals line is its text alternative,
   and the per-bucket <title> tooltips are a mouse-only extra. #}
{%- if spark is not null -%}
{% set vw = constant('App\\Dashboard\\NetworkUsageChart::WIDTH') %}
{% set vh = constant('App\\Dashboard\\NetworkUsageChart::HEIGHT') %}
<div class="unifi-spark">
  <div class="d-flex justify-content-end text-secondary small">
    ↓ {{ spark.downTotal }} · ↑ {{ spark.upTotal }}
  </div>
  <svg class="unifi-chart" style="height:48px" viewBox="0 0 {{ vw }} {{ vh }}" preserveAspectRatio="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <polygon class="unifi-chart-fill" points="{{ spark.downArea }}"/>
    <polyline class="unifi-chart-down" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" points="{{ spark.downLine }}"/>
    <polyline class="unifi-chart-up" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke" points="{{ spark.upLine }}"/>
    {% for p in spark.points %}
      <rect x="{{ p.x }}" y="0" width="{{ p.w }}" height="{{ vh }}" fill="transparent"><title>{{ p.label }}</title></rect>
    {% endfor %}
  </svg>
  <div class="unifi-chart-axis">
    <span>{{ spark.startLabel }}</span><span>{{ spark.endLabel }}</span>
  </div>
</div>
{%- endif -%}
